MID_SE_Led_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_001: Oh, hey, Mu. Looks like you've been training.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_002: Yep, I sure have! I want to get really strong so I can\nbe just like you, Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_003: I'm not that strong, you know.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_004: But you saved me, remember? And besides, you're\njust...just...
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_005: so grown-up and sophisticated and...beautiful.\nBasically, you're perfect.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_006: Heh. You're so innocent, Mu. It's nice.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_007: {SetColor=Gray}She's been through so much. I can't just leave her\nto figure this all out alone.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_008: But listen, you are a bit careless. It seems like you're\nalways getting into some kind of trouble.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_009: I guess. But that's why I dress like a boy—\nto protect myself.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_010: Anyone with a decent eye can see right through your\nprotection. Sirocco figured it out immediately.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_011: Ughhh. Yeah, maybe you're right.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_012: Look, Mu, danger is everywhere. You must never\never let your guard down.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_013: More importantly, you should learn to manipulate any\nman you meet—twist them right around your finger.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_014: Oh, OK. If that'll make me more like you, then I'll\ndo that.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_015: Nyeh!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_016: Sounds like all that training made you hungry.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_017: Hehehe... Heh... So embarrassing. Guess I'm\nnowhere near as sophisticated as you.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_018: Come on, let's get something to eat. My treat.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_019: Oh wow, thanks! See, that's what I mean. You just\nsay stuff and do stuff with so much confidence.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_020: I'm going to order whatever you order. If I eat like\nyou, maybe I'll be more like you.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_C_021: I don't think eating like me is what you should focus\non. How about you just order what you like, OK?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_001: Oh, Leda! Great timing! I was just looking for you.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_002: Hey, you're back again today. You've been hanging\naround a lot lately.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_003: Hehe... Sorry. It's because I love spending time with\nyou, Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_004: Hmhm. OK, if you say so. Um, do you need\nsomething?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_005: Oh, right, yeah. I want to learn to play a musical\ninstrument.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_006: You're this incredible singer and dancer... I mean,\nyou're the Rose of Caelus!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_007: I know I'm not a noble like you are, but I'm going to\ndo whatever I can to be more like you.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_008: {SetColor=Gray}Ugh... I wish she wouldn't say things like that. She\nthinks I'm...good. I'm not good at all.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_009: Leda?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_010: I was just thinking that it's pretty late for you to\nstart learning to play an instrument.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_011: By the time I was your age, I had already won the\nRose of Caelus title.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_012: Wow! I mean, that's amazing... You're amazing.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_013: But I can't let that stop me from trying. How else am\nI going to be like you?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_014: Stop it. Just...stop trying to imitate me. It's for your\nown good, Mu.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_015: What does that mean? Why would you say that?!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_016: Because. Just be a good kid, and do as you're told.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_017: But...I owe you my life, and I look up to you!\nWhat's wrong with wanting to be like you?!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_018: I don't care if it's you who's telling me not to be\nlike you. I'm not going to listen to...to...YOU!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_019: Alright. OK. Thank you for saying exactly what you\nthink, Mu. You're such an honest kid.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_020: But that's exactly why you shouldn't use me as some\nkind of role model.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_021: Stop it! Stop telling me what to do and how to feel!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_022: I've admired you since I met you, Leda! And I'll\nnever stop!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_023: She admires me so much she thinks my desire for\nrevenge is OK. She's so innocent...and so vulnerable.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_B_024: Just stay the way you are, Mu. Please, don't you ever\nbecome anything like me.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_001: Uhh, so this finger goes here, that one goes there...\nYeah, I think that looks right.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_002: She's practicing the vihuela. Really practicing.\nI've got to make her stop this.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_003: Now that I've got some fingering figured out, maybe\nI'll try to play a song all the way through. Here goes!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_004: Wow, that is not great. I know she just started\nlearning, but still—she's awful.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_005: She looks like she's having a great time though...\nlike she really enjoys playing.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_006: I used to be like that. I'd get so absorbed in the music\nthat I'd play until the sun went down.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_007: Phew. I stumbled in a few places, but I did a lot\nbetter than I thought I would. Yay for me!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_008: Oh, hi, Leda! Were you listening?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_009: I was. Are you playing the vihuela because that's\nwhat I play?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_010: Yep! You told me to stop trying to be like you, but\nI'm not doing that. I figured I'd just learn on my own.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_011: Vihuelas are expensive. So I found a broken one\nthat had been tossed out, and I fixed it.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_012: I really don't know how to play it properly, but it\ndoesn't matter. It's still fun!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_013: Well, you must be bored if this is how you want to\nspend your time.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_014: Not really, but I am confused about how to play some\nof the chords. Would you...give me some tips?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_015: The best way to learn is from someone who's super\nskilled. How about it? Will you help me?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_016: Ugh, how are you like this? How do you keep coming\nback when I've pushed you away so many times?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_017: See! You didn't say no! And that's because the person\nI owe my life to—my role model—is kind and good.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_018: You cheeky little thing. You really are unstoppable,\nyou know that?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_019: I guess that makes me feel better. With that kind of\ntenacity, you'll...probably turn out alright.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_020: What do you mean "probably turn out alright"?
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_021: Never mind. Look, even if I did say no to helping\nyou, you'd keep pestering me anyway.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_022: So fine, I'll teach you how to play properly. Hand me\nthat vihuela.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_023: Eeeee! Really?! YES!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_024: By the way, you are so much worse at this than you\nthink you are.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_025: And since you begged me to teach you, I won't\ntolerate any complaining, and I won't go easy.
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_026: I can take anything you throw at me!
MID_SE_Led_Moo_A_027: Hehehe. I know you can.